§9.1/D-10: a decorator line reads its head in exactly one order — `@@type` →
slot → `{specs}` → `%%numbering` — and every part lands on the block it
decorates:

@@quoteA[intro]("Aside title"){.q, #q1, k: "v"}%%%numberA
> a quote configured by one decorator line

The `%%` run carries its own depth (`%%%` = depth 2), so the marker names a
`[[task.number.custom]]` counter rather than the element's (§10.5).

The sigil, not the type, is what makes a line a decorator: the untyped form
carries a slot and a numbering marker just the same:

@@[intro2]%%numberA
> a quote decorated without a type
